<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Cairns hike planner" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
  <metadata>
    <name>Wallace Falls</name>
    <desc>Wallace Falls trailhead to the Upper Falls and back. 8.2 km, +445 m, −443 m.</desc>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="47.867017" lon="-121.678106">
    <ele>101.9</ele>
    <name>1 Wallace Falls trailhead</name>
    <desc>State park: Discover Pass, or buy a day pass at the machine in the lot. From October the park opens at 8:00 and closes at dusk. Restrooms at the lot; carry 1–1.5 L each. About 100 spaces: full by late morning on weekends, quiet on weekdays.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.866636" lon="-121.671516">
    <ele>110.6</ele>
    <name>2 Railroad Grade junction</name>
    <desc>Under the power lines. Keep right on the Woody Trail, along the river. The Railroad Grade to the left is a gentler old logging grade, about 1.5 km longer, that rejoins before the falls.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.872817" lon="-121.654512">
    <ele>265.5</ele>
    <name>3 Lower Falls picnic shelter</name>
    <desc>The first falls, with a shelter and benches. Eat now: the switchbacks above here are the steep part, about 250 m of climb in 1.4 km.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.873999" lon="-121.649611">
    <ele>402.9</ele>
    <name>4 Middle Falls viewpoint</name>
    <desc>The big one: the tallest of the three falls, in full view. The Skykomish Valley overlook is a few switchbacks higher. Steep drop-offs at the viewpoints: stay on the trail, and keep children close.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.876507" lon="-121.646368">
    <ele>507.5</ele>
    <name>5 Upper Falls</name>
    <desc>The top of the Woody Trail, beside the Upper Falls. The old road beyond goes on toward Wallace Lake; turn around here.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.873999" lon="-121.649611">
    <ele>402.9</ele>
    <name>6 Middle Falls (down)</name>
    <desc>Steep, stepped trail down to the picnic shelter: slick when wet. Short steps; poles help.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.872817" lon="-121.654512">
    <ele>265.5</ele>
    <name>7 Lower Falls shelter (down)</name>
    <desc>The rest is gentle: along the river and back across the North Fork bridge.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.866636" lon="-121.671516">
    <ele>110.6</ele>
    <name>8 Railroad Grade junction (down)</name>
    <desc>Straight on under the power lines to the lot.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.867017" lon="-121.678106">
    <ele>101.9</ele>
    <name>9 Wallace Falls trailhead</name>
    <desc>Finish. Back at the car.</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>Milestone</type>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>Wallace Falls</name>
